{
  "title": "Projectile Target Challenge: Pick Angle and Speed",
  "description": "A launcher sits at the left end of a flat 70 m field with distance marks every 10 m. A blue target disc 3 m across (a hit window of 1.5 m either side of centre) with a yellow flag sits down the field. Set the launch angle and speed, then press Launch: the orange ball flies its arc, leaving a trail. Your previous arc stays as a faded grey path. Readouts show landing distance, miss distance and side, flight time, highest point, launches used and targets hit.",
  "experience": "game",
  "behavior": "rules",
  "controlProfile": "inspect",
  "stepped": true,
  "game": {
    "objective": "Hit 3 targets (at 30 m, 45 m, then 18 m) using no more than 10 launches. A landing within 1.5 m of the target centre, edges included, is a hit.",
    "hint": "At the same speed, angles that add to 90° (like 30° and 60°) land at the same distance, and 45° goes farthest. Doubling the speed makes the shot go four times as far."
  },
