  "assumptions": [
    "Simplified simulation: no air resistance, and the ball starts at ground level on flat ground.",
    "Gravity is 9.8 m/s² straight down; the sideways speed stays constant and only the vertical speed changes.",
    "Each point of the flight is computed exactly from the projectile formulas, so the landing distance equals speed² × sin(2 × angle) ÷ 9.8.",
    "The ball is treated as a point (drawn larger so you can see it); the flight ends when it returns to ground height.",
    "Targets come in a fixed order (30 m, 45 m, 18 m); Reset starts the same challenge again and clears the score and trails.",
    "Every flight is shown over about two seconds of screen time, so screen time does not match the flight-time readout. Real balls are slowed by air and land shorter."
  ],
